# Build-context rules for Dockerfile.compiler ONLY.
#
# BuildKit looks for "<path to Dockerfile>.dockerignore" before falling back to
# "<context>/.dockerignore". This file exists to make one targeted exception to
# the root rules: deploy/testdata must reach THIS image, because Render has no
# volume to mount it from. Everything else stays excluded, including — most
# importantly — the .env files.
#
# If a builder ever ignores this convention and falls back to the root file, the
# COPY of deploy/testdata fails and the build stops with "file not found". That
# is the correct failure: a judge silently shipped without its test cases would
# report every submission as an internal error instead.

# Secrets. Never relax these. Handed over as environment variables at run time.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.sample

# Rebuilt inside the image by npm ci; the host's copies are also compiled for
# the wrong architecture.
**/node_modules

# Nothing below is needed to compile or judge.
frontend
backend
scripts
csnotes
cses_problems
compiler/testdata
compiler/problems
compiler/codes
compiler/outputs
.git
**/*.md
**/.DS_Store
**/*.log
**/*.bak
